test_distance_field -- compute / distance_field, vertex and facet (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_distance_field_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     8 decks, about 30 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  compute / distance_field / mo_sink / mo_src / dfield / facet gives,
  for every vertex of mo_sink, the exact distance to the nearest point
  of the cells of mo_src: inside a triangle, on an edge or at a vertex.
  mo_src holds triangles and line segments, or quads only (cut into 4
  triangles at their centers by hextotet / 4). Without the sixth word,
  or with vertex, the command gives the distance to the nearest vertex
  of mo_src, as before.

  The checker computes every distance again by brute force in plain
  Python (standard library): for each sink vertex, the facets nearest
  bounding sphere first, each by projection onto its plane when that
  falls inside the triangle, else the nearest of the three edges;
  written independently of the Fortran (closest_pt_tri_lg.f, the
  barycentric regions). They must agree to 1e-10 of the source's size
  (the AVS files carry about 12 digits).

  df01  one tilted triangle; a 13^3 grid of sink points around it hits
        every face, edge and vertex region; 7 points on the triangle
        (its vertices, edge midpoints, centroid) must give 0; and a
        dense sample of the triangle (20,301 points) must never be
        closer than LaGriT's answer (an independent upper bound)
  df02  a sphere of 320 triangles, 1500 random sink points; the vertex
        option in the same run: equal to the brute-force nearest
        vertex, never smaller than the facet distance
  df03  a warped quad surface (36 quads, not planar)
  df04  a helix of 80 line segments
  df05  8 triangles and 2 line segments in one mesh object
  df06  the vertex option with 5 words and with 6 words (vertex):
        identical, and equal to the brute-force nearest vertex
  df07  refused, with an ERROR and no attribute made: a tet source,
        quads mixed with triangles, a source with no cells, a sixth
        word that is not vertex or facet; the next command works
  df08  a sphere of 5120 triangles and a 41^3 grid of sink points
        (68921); brute force on every 10th sink vertex

FILES

  run_distance_field_tests.sh   runs the decks, then the checker
  make_distance_inputs.py       writes the AVS inputs into work/
  df*.lgi                       the LaGriT decks
  check_distance_field.py       brute-force checks, SVG pictures, summary
  work/, logs/                  made by the run (not in git)
